<!--
  Phase 5e derived legacy WEB-INF/web.xml insert.

  This block is added verbatim to the frozen Phase 5b descriptor, immediately
  before its <filter> declaration of requestFilter. Nothing else in that
  descriptor is touched, so the derived archive's descriptor is provably
  "the frozen text plus exactly this block" - which is what
  verifyPhase5eDerivedLegacyWar recomputes rather than trusts.

  Why here, and not appended:

    * Filter order in a deployment descriptor is declaration order, and the
      Phase 5e router must run BEFORE SessionTimeoutFilter. That filter refuses
      a request whose session was never registered, and the router has to see -
      and reject - a forged internal header even on such a request.
    * The Servlet 2.4 schema models <web-app> as an unbounded choice, so element
      order is free; inserting at the existing filter position is chosen for
      readability of the resulting descriptor, not for validity.

  Session tracking is pinned to cookies by REPLACING the frozen <session-config>
  element (see gradle/phase5/derived-web-xml-session-config.xml), not by adding
  a second one: two <session-config> elements are accepted by the Servlet 2.4
  choice model but their merge behaviour is container-specific, and a descriptor
  whose meaning depends on the container is not a contract.

  One honest caveat about <tracking-mode> in a version="2.4" descriptor: the
  element was introduced by Servlet 3.0, so it is not in the 2.4 schema. Tomcat
  registers its digester rule for session-config/tracking-mode unconditionally
  rather than per descriptor version, and runs with xmlValidation="false" by
  default, so the element IS honoured here. The descriptor version is
  deliberately left at 2.4: raising it to 3.0 would additionally enable
  web-fragment and annotation scanning for the frozen archive, which is a far
  larger behavioural change than the one being made. verifyPhase5eDerivedLegacyWar
  asserts the version did not move.
-->
	<listener>
		<description>
			Phase 5e: initialises the cohort bridge and refuses to deploy a
			partially registered Phase 5e overlay.
		</description>
		<display-name>ADempiere Phase 5e Cohort Bridge</display-name>
		<listener-class>
			org.adempiere.web.bridge.CohortBridgeStartupListener
		</listener-class>
	</listener>

	<filter>
		<filter-name>phase5eCohortRouter</filter-name>
		<filter-class>org.adempiere.web.bridge.CohortRoutingFilter</filter-class>
	</filter>
	<filter-mapping>
		<filter-name>phase5eCohortRouter</filter-name>
		<url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
	</filter-mapping>

